u}{3}$ for baryon number) and is typically derived from statistical mechanics and relates to the inverse of the entropy density in units of temperature cubed, a common approximation at high temperatures where the energy density is dominated by relativistic particles. The factor $7.04$ arises from specific assumptions about the particle content and degrees of freedom in the system, often related to the Stefan-Boltzmann law for a plasma of quarks, gluons, and other relativistic particles.
